This file is tracked on purpose, and it is the only thing in frontend/dist
that is.

gui.go embeds this directory with `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`, and a Go
embed pattern that matches no files is a compile error — so without something
tracked here, `go install github.com/otis-http/otis@latest` would fail to
build, because the bundle itself is generated and never committed.

With it, that install produces a working `otis` command whose window declines
to open and says why (gui.go's assetsPresent). The way to install only the
command line, with no frontend and no cgo, is:

    go install -tags otis_cli github.com/otis-http/otis@latest
